WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.720
Your new favorite show, House of the Dragon,
Game of Thrones Prequel series is currently

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.990
filming and is coming in 2022 on HBO.

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:12.960
Based on George RR Martin’s book Fire And
Blood, it tells the story of the Dance of

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:19.050
the Dragons, a Targaryen civil war of succession
between Aegon II and his half-sister Rhaenyra

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.640
over their father Viserys I's throne.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.070
These days you are able to see many House
of the Dragon set photos, which serve as a

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.619
little promo or tease for what is about to
come.

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:35.530
Rhaenyra Targaryen and Daemon Targaryen are
the only characters we see in these photos.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:40.730
Here you can see them filming on the set that’s
been in production for the past week on Holywell

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:41.920
Beach in Cornwall.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.989
They are in full regal Targaryen costume.

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:50.489
They shared a scene, speaking together on
the beach, and once they finished their conversation,

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:54.350
Rhaenyra then walked towards the sea which
is when the scene ends.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:59.399
Rhaenyra and Daemon are on Driftmark, the
seat of House Velayrion and this scene takes

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:02.579
place after the bloody Battle of the Gullet.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:04.559
So who are these two characters?

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:08.590
Rhaenyra and Daemon are the main characters
of our story.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:13.500
King Viserys’ chosen heir, a dragon rider
who grew up expecting to become the first

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.049
ruling Queen of Westeros.

00:01:16.049 --> 00:01:21.299
Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen, cheered as the
Realm's Delight when she was young and later

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:27.590
called the Half-Year Queen, was the first-born
child of King Viserys I Targaryen.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:33.630
Rhaenyra was King Viserys I's only living
child by his first wife, Queen Aemma of House

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:34.719
Arryn.

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:40.340
At the age of eight she was made her father's
heir and grew up expecting to become the first

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.610
ruling Queen of Westeros.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:46.189
Rhaenyra was a dragonrider whose mount was
Syrax.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:52.210
Rhaenyra had her family's Valyrian looks,
wearing her silver-gold hair in a long braid

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:55.950
in the manner of Queen Visenya Targaryen.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.890
Beautiful as a child, Rhaenyra was later declared
by her uncle, later husband and the man who

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:06.540
is standing beside her in these photos, Prince
Daemon Targaryen, to be the most beautiful

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.349
maiden in all the Seven Kingdoms.

00:02:09.349 --> 00:02:14.379
Daemon Targaryen is also a key figure from
this time period and is George R.R. Martin's

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:16.620
favorite Targaryen.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:21.690
Daemon Targaryen also known as Prince of the
City, Lord Flea Bottom and the Rogue Prince

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:27.530
had many titles throughout his life: Prince,
Ser, Commander of the City Watch, Master of

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:33.819
coin, master of laws, King of the stepstones
and the narrow sea, protector of the realm.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:40.010
Daemon was the most contoversial man of his
lifetime, an audacious rogue prince and adventuer

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:43.569
who seemed made of good and evil in equal
measure.

00:02:43.569 --> 00:02:48.560
There was never a man so loved and so reviled,
and at a same time, as he was.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:53.769
During the Dance of the Dragons, as the husband
of his niece Rhaenyra, he supported his wife's

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:59.099
claim, and he was considered by many the most
dangerous man in Westeros.

00:02:59.099 --> 00:03:04.250
He was Rhaenyra's second husband, following
Ser Laenor Velaryon and she was his third

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.250
wife.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:10.030
Prince Daemon was the most experienced warrior
of his time and wielded the Valyrian steel

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.070
blade Dark Sister.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:18.110
A dragonrider whose dragon was Caraxes, Daemon
declared himself the King of the Stepstones

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:19.989
and the Narrow Sea.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:25.290
Daemon was a skilled warrior, described in
the histories as dashing, daring, and dangerous.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:31.840
He was also ambitious, impetuous, mercurial,
amoral, reckless, and quick to take offense.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:35.290
He is described as being as charming as he
was hot-tempered.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:42.150
Due to the lack of a male heir, Viserys designated
Rhaenyra as his successor.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:47.450
Therefore, Rhaenyra was the only female Targaryen
to lay claim to the Iron Throne in her own

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.530
right.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:54.470
Since she was raised as the designated heir,
Rhaenyra became quite pampered and arrogant,

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:57.930
but also gained practical governmental experience.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:05.280
After Rhaenyra's mother died, her father remarried
and had several sons by his second wife, Alicent

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.110
of House Hightower.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:12.530
Even so, Viserys still publicly expected his
daughter to succeed him, and when he died,

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.050
his official will even stated so.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:19.970
However, Rhaenyra's younger half-brother,
Aegon, challenged her claim.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:25.070
He stated that the normal inheritance laws
of the Andals (which formed the basis of the

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:32.150
unified law code in Westeros) called for male-preference
primogeniture, meaning that a younger son

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:35.600
would rightfully inherit before an older daughter.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.690
Rhaenyra had 2 husbands and 5 sons.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:43.160
Her fist husband was Laenor of House Velayrion,
son of the Sea Snake.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:49.690
Laenor and Rhaenyra had three sons together:
Princes Jacaerys 'Jace', Lucerys 'Luke', and

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:50.890
Joffrey 'Joff' Velaryon.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:56.160
All were near adulthood and had dragons of
their own when Rhaenyra's father, Viserys

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.180
I, died.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:02.500
It was rumored that those sons of Rhaenyra's
were actually fathered by her champion and

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:08.320
lover, Harwin Strong, the strongest man in
Westeros, called "Breakbones", as all three

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:14.070
were born with brown hair and brown eyes,
though Laenor and Rhaenyra both had light

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.720
silver/gold hair and purple eyes.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.340
The Greens were the ones who sparked this
ruomor, often calling them Strongs.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:26.190
The true parentage of Rhaenyra's three eldest
children is still unclear.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:31.280
The siblings Laenor and Laena Velaryon who
were married to Rhaenyra and Daemon Targaryen,

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:37.160
both died in 120 AC, as did Rhaenyra's alleged
lover, Breakbones.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:42.370
Rhaenyra then secretly married her uncle,
Prince Daemon, the most experienced and the

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.770
most dangerous warrior of his time, at Dragonstone.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:51.620
The news of their wedding caused a great scandal
at the court of King's Landing and made Rhaenyra's

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.180
father furious.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.060
It took some time before Viserys and Daemon
reconciled.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:06:02.530
Rhaenyra's other sons, Princes Aegon and Viserys
Targaryen, were fathered by Daemon and all

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:03.990
had Targaryen features.

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:09.830
At the time of her father's death, Rhaenyra
was on Dragonstone awaiting the birth of her

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:10.990
child.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:15.830
The greens in King's Landing ensured that
the news of the Viserys's death did not reach

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:22.080
her until her own supporters in the Red Keep
were dead or imprisoned and Aegon II's coronation

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.490
had already occurred.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:29.360
This began a devastating civil war that tore
apart the Seven Kingdoms, known as The Dance

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:35.180
of the Dragons, as it was the only war in
which both sides had dragonriders.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:40.550
These scenes right here take place after the
bloodiest sea battle in Westeros history.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:45.990
There is an upturned shipwrecked hull being
set up by carpenters on the location.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:50.680
The presence of a leftover shipwreck as many
of you guessed correctly points to the Battle

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.900
of the Gullet.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:56.750
The Battle of the Gullet, also called the
Battle in the Gullet, was a battle that took

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:01.400
place in the Gullet in 130 AC during the Dance
of the Dragons.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.390
It remains among the bloodiest sea battles
in all of history.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:11.460
House Velaryon blockaded the Gullet and controlled
access to Blackwater Bay at the start of the

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.460
civil war.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:18.550
After the assault on Harrenhal by Prince Daemon
Targaryen and further blows to the greens,

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:24.160
Ser Otto Hightower, the Hand of the King to
Aegon II Targaryen, hatched a plan to break

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:26.090
the Velaryon fleet's blockade.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:31.180
Otto reached out across the narrow sea to
enemies of Prince Daemon, the Triarchy, hoping

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:36.440
to persuade them to move against the Sea Snake,
Lord Corlys Velaryon.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:42.110
Otto's plan took time and Aegon II eventually
ran out of patience with his grandfather's

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:47.260
prevarications, replacing him as Hand with
Ser Criston Cole.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:52.400
The schemes of Otto eventually bore fruit,
as the High Council of the Triarchy accepted

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.180
his offer of alliance in Tyrosh.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:59.620
Ninety warships, commanded swept from the
Stepstones under the banners of the Three

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:03.290
Daughters, bending their oars for the Gullet.

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:07.460
Meanwhile on Dragonstone, it was decided by
Prince Jacaerys Velaryon that his half-brothers,

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:13.810
Princes Aegon and Viserys Targaryen, would
be fostered with a Prince of Pentos until

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:18.250
their mother, Queen Rhaenyra Targaryen, had
secured the Iron Throne.

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:22.860
The princes departed on a ship, towards the
end of 129 AC.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:27.460
The Sea Snake sent seven of his warships with
them as escort.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:32.620
Their ships encountered the Triarchy's fleet,
which had sailed up to the Gullet.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:36.350
It was taken captive and warships were sunk
or captured.

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:42.159
Possessed only of a dragon egg, Viserys had
no way of escaping from the ship and was made

00:08:42.159 --> 00:08:43.159
captive.

00:08:43.159 --> 00:08:46.780
Aegon escaped on his young dragon, Stormcloud.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:52.630
Sailors attempted to bring them down and Stormcloud
was wounded by arrows and scorpion bolts.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:57.510
Nevertheless, they flew to Dragonstone, where
Aegon delivered the news of the threat from

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:58.640
the east.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.700
Stormcloud died at Dragonstone from his wounds.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:06.270
The battle began on the fifth day of the new
year, 130 AC.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:11.570
The Triarchy's ships divided into two squadrons
entering the Gullet to the north and south

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.010
of Dragonstone.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:17.410
They attacked at sunrise, surprising House
Velaryon's fleet.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:23.090
Flying on Vermax to meet the fleet of the
Triarchy, Prince Jacaerys Velaryon swept down

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.980
upon enemy galleys.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:30.690
The sailors had experience fighting Prince
Daemon Targaryen and his dragon, Caraxes,

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:35.470
during the war for the Stepstones, so their
captains directed their spears and arrows

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.380
against Jacaerys.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:41.350
One ship caught on fire and then another,
however.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:46.250
When Jacaerys was joined by Ulf the White
on Silverwing, Nettles on Sheepstealer, Addam

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:52.670
Velaryon on Seasmoke, and Hugh Hammer on Vermithor,
the line of warships from the Free Cities

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:55.980
shattered as one galley after another turned
away.

00:09:55.980 --> 00:10:01.550
Vermax flew too low, however, and crashed
down into the sea, possibly wounded from a

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:05.880
crossbow bolt to the eye or pulled down by
a grapnel.

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:10.340
Survivors said he struggled in the rigging
of a burning galley and sank with it.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:15.330
Jacaerys leaped free, but was then killed
by Myrish crossbowmen.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:19.500
North and south of Dragonstone the battle
continued into nighttime.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:25.150
The southern squadron bypassed Dragonstone,
believing that it was too strong to assault,

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:31.380
and instead attacked Driftmark, setting afire
the harbor of Spicetown with fire ships.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.680
The town was sacked, with its inhabitants
butchered.

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:39.940
The High Tide and the treasures of Lord Corlys
Velaryon were burned by Myrish and Tyroshi

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:44.290
soldiers, with the Sea Snake's servants cut
down as they fled.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:49.330
These scenes here take place a day or two
after that as Rhaenyra and Daemon return to

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:53.830
see what's left of Driftmark, discussing their
next moves.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:58.230
I hope these photos of Rhaenyra and Demon
Targaryen made you even more excited for the

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:02.470
upcoming epic Game of Thrones prequel series,
House of the Dragon.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:07.900
Thank you so much for watching and I hope
to see you in the next one.

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:10.670
Peace!

